A||||8||Shaun41178||Another race||||14||
Z||000000||Shaun41178||12-11-1999||04:54 AM||||Out tonight cruising looking for some action.  I saw a 4th gen Camaro go by so I pull a u-turn to catch up.  I finally do at a light and I see the dual exhaust of a Z28.  So I am like cool.  I have been beaten by 4th gen Z's before but they are good competition.  So I am behind the Z as we pull away from the light and I see the Z jumping on the gas real quick and backing off.  Must be from the manual tranny.  I couldn't figure out why this guy was doing that.  I must have been oblivious cause I looked over and saw that the Z was jumping at a Sn-95 GT.  The guy in the Z kept jumping it but nothing so the Z sped ahead.  So I pull up quick and start jumping my car at the Stang to see if he would go with me.  I hear the Stang rev up so I punch it.  While waiting for my tranny to downshift he pulled a bumper and that is where it stayed from about 40-75 mph.  We were dead even.  Neither of us could pull.  This stang must have been modded cause I have raced a 4.6 GT before and whooped it bad.  It makes me wonder what he had.  I would guess the stang was a mid 14 second car.  I was coming up fast on the Z that has spead ahead so I had to brake and the Stang stayed on it so I pulled in behind the Stang and wanted to follow but the stang ran through a yellow light and I was not about to run it.  I followed the Z a bit trying to get next to him but never could and he pulled into a gas station so I continued on my way.  I guess the stang driver knew he would have his ass handed to him by the Z so he tried to race something he was sure he could beat.  I probably surprised him.  I can see him now scratching his head.  Hehe<P>About to retire for the night I see a neon with a 3 foot high wing on the back like a supra or something so I go after it.  I hate rice.  The Neon is making its way onto a two lane road so I decide not to pursue and as I was turning a corner I see a 3rd gen camaro at a light so I quickly turn around and lucky for me I am able to get up next to him as traffic had lightened up.  I pulled up along side and noticed he had dual exhaust with custom tips and the ground effects of an Iroc however it didn't say iroc on the car by the front tire nor did it say RS or anything like that.  I roll my window down and ask the passenger if they wanted to run it.  Apparently the guy didn't know what I was talking about cause he responded with "run it to where?"  So I said want to race?  The driver kind if just sat there not saying anything but the passenger was being an idiot.  He said<BR>"You only have a Fiero, We have a Camaro.  We are going to kill you!"<P>Me: "Well why don't we race and find out whose car is faster"<P>I love it when people talk smack not knowing what they are getting themselves into.  Light turned green and I started out slow to see if they were going to go.  The driver did not punch it off the line but eased into it and at 15 mph he puched it so I did as well not knowing what he had under the hood.  I pulled a car quickly and shut down for them to catch up.  Well he does so I punch it again and leave them another quick car behind.  I started luaghing now cause it kind of occured to me that he probably has an RS with a 305 TBi engine.  So I just kept playing with him.  I would slow down and keep jumping it waiting for him to go and then I would pull a quick car and do it again.  This happened about 5 times or so.  Everytime I would let them get next to me I would look over but they never looked over at me.  So I give them a thumbs up but they are not looking.  Must be embarresed.  I would be for sure especially talking smack about a car and then getting your @ss handed to you.  LOL.  So finally I had enough fun embarressing them so I gave it a big rev to 5 grand as I was alongside of them and then continued on my way home.<P>Pick up the Feb issue of HPP.  There is a 455 powered Fiero pulling a wheelie.  Cool stuff.||||reg||14
Z||000001||88formula||12-11-1999||09:35 PM||||Did you beat him with nitrous? What are your mod's if any? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||12-11-1999||10:27 PM||||hey shaun i will vouch for you, i was at a light, to my left new stang, to my right, new chevy v6 truck.being that i have only had this car and rebuilt it(engine)for 3 months, and driving a trans am, i thought i'll probably lose.so then i thought what the heck let's see what she will do,we pulled out and i kicked ther ass hard, i couldn't believe what happened, so at the next light i tryed it again, same outcome. the stang didn't even want to catch up after the 2 time and the truck well he just vanished, so you see these fieros have good kick if you take care of them properly.long live the fiero!!!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||12-12-1999||05:38 PM||||I may have said this before, but the fact is that any car can be fast with nitrous.  I'm not trying to slam or anything, but did you beat the Camaro with or without nitrous? When you can take an LT1 without nitrous, THEN I will worship you, man.  I'm just waiting for the post that says "Blew my engine after getting happy with nitrous."<BR>hehe.... good kills Shaun.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||12-12-1999||11:55 PM||||So what are you saying, GT Bastard?  If I put nitrous on my neighbors Yugo, can I beat a Corvette?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||12-13-1999||12:42 AM||||Nitrous may seem like cheating to some people, but think about the hp/cost ratio.  It is one of the most cost-effective ways to make your car go faster.  The camaro guy could get nitrous just as easy and be even faster..  ||||reg||4
Z||000006||Shaun41178||12-13-1999||03:47 AM||||Wow, i think this is the most posts that any of my race stories have gotten.  Anyways....<P>88 Formula:  Mods consist of nitrous, underdrive pulley, and ported exhaust manifolds.  Yes I did beat the Camaro with nitrous although looking back now I didn't need my nitrous.  His car was a dog.  I was at 3/4 throttle and I was still able to pull him.  i just used it to make it even more embaressing for the guy.<P>GT basterd:  No flame taken.  I know you have a 4th gen Z as I believe you also post on the Camaro board.  Perhaps with my future 3.2(now in progress) I could probably run mid to high 14's without nitrous.  However the fact remains I still won't be able to hang with a stock Lt-1 unless of course the driver is terrible.  You said you will worship me if I can beat an Lt-1 without nitrous.  What if I use a supercharger or Turbo?  Will that not count?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">)  True my engine might blow up but at least I would do it having fun.  HEHE<BR>I know I don't have the fastest car but I love having nitrous.  It makes me a contender now with some of the f-bods out there.  From a roll I get pounded but from a stop I am pretty competitive.  I have run a best of 8.8 in the 1/8th with consistent 8.9-9.0.  That is just as good or better as many Lt-1's out there.  I got my nitrous to surprise many drivers out there and to teach them to never underestimate a Fiero andI have done that.  So I guess part of that mission is complete.  The new mission to to build a faster car and have more power because I am now a speed freak.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||12-13-1999||04:15 PM||||What happens if the engine blows? You'll lose you speed.  all thats left is fr--- Naw you own a Fiero. Your cool||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||12-13-1999||08:43 PM||||Adding high performance parts to your car is cheating? Then a Fiero with a big V8 is one big S.O.B. of a cheater. There's an old saying my Daddy used to say: All's fair in war and racing, but nothing's fair about love (or something like that)!||||reg||1
